From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 06:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] s: use the Bellatrix DWC2 host driver

The Emu68 port now owns a dedicated DWC2 driver.  Select it for Poseidon while
leaving the earlier usb2otg integration patch intact until the replacement has
completed its distribution-level validation.
---
 workbench/s/Startup-Sequence | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence b/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
index 8a2aef5f81..92a57ad863 100644
--- a/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
+++ b/workbench/s/Startup-Sequence
@@ -120,8 +120,19 @@
 ; starts the stack and restores saved preferences, but a machine that has never
 ; had Poseidon configured has no hardware in them. Tell it about the controller
 ; that is actually present, if one is.
+; Either host controller, whichever the build put here.
+;
+; There are two, both ours: dwc2emu68 is the Bellatrix driver and usb2otg is
+; the adopted AROS engine (ISSUE-0047). Naming only one meant the other could
+; never be booted, so it could never be compared -- and comparing them is the
+; whole point of keeping both. build-aros.sh leaves exactly one on the card.
+If EXISTS "DEVS:USBHardware/dwc2emu68.device"
+    Echo "starting AddUSBHardware dwc2emu68" >"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+    AddUSBHardware DEVS:USBHardware/dwc2emu68.device >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+    Echo "finished AddUSBHardware" >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+EndIf
 If EXISTS "DEVS:USBHardware/usb2otg.device"
-    Echo "starting AddUSBHardware" >"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
+    Echo "starting AddUSBHardware usb2otg" >"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
     AddUSBHardware DEVS:USBHardware/usb2otg.device >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
     Echo "finished AddUSBHardware" >>"SDCARD0P0:usb-hardware.log"
 EndIf
